course: dictionary
lesson: 13563
title: Inaction: doing nothing when action is needed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inaction means not doing anything, especially when something should be done. It is a noun, so you can say «inaction» the way you say «the silence» or «the wait». Look at its parts: in- means not, and action means doing something. So inaction is not doing.
explain: Use the context to check. «The council took no action for months, so the broken bridge stayed broken. Their inaction made the problem worse.» The sentence tells you that nobody fixed the bridge, so inaction means not acting. Swap in «not doing anything» and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Inaction is not always neutral. «Ella saw a boy being bullied and walked on. Her inaction hurt him.» Doing nothing is still a choice, and it can have consequences for other people. In stories, a character's inaction can lead to trouble, so readers notice when someone fails to act.
explain: Listen for phrases you will meet in news and citizenship lessons: a period of inaction, inaction on a problem, criticised for inaction. People criticise «inaction on climate change» when governments do not act to solve it.
fact: Inaction means not doing anything, especially when something should be done.
fact: The prefix in- means not, so inaction is the opposite of action.
fact: Inaction is a noun, and you can say «a period of inaction».
fact: To be «criticised for inaction» means people say you should have acted and you did not.
fact: Choosing to do nothing can still have consequences, so inaction is a kind of choice.
exercise: «The council's inaction left the bridge broken for months.» What does inaction mean here? | Painting the bridge bright red | *Not doing anything when action was needed | Building something new and strong | Arguing loudly at a meeting
exercise: People criticise «inaction on climate change». What are they upset about? | Children playing outside in the sun | Scientists doing too many experiments | Governments holding too many parties | *Governments not acting on the problem
exercise: Which word means doing nothing when action is needed? | *Inaction | Action | Interaction | Reaction
test: Why is doing nothing in the bullying example still a choice? | Because it is always the best way to help | *Because doing nothing still has consequences for others | Because it means running away fast | Because it only happens in stories
test: In «a period of inaction», what does the phrase tell you? | A time when everyone played sport | *A time when nothing was done | A time when the weather was very cold | A time of loud music and dancing
exam: Which sentence uses inaction correctly? | *The team's inaction let the problem get worse while everyone waited. | Inaction is a fast and happy runner. | They inaction the old car yesterday. | Her inaction jumped over the wall and ran home.
